cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalisation, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "OddCycleBound: A Lean 4 formalisation of Goodman-type lower bounds for odd cycles I: The dense regime"
authors:
  - family-names: Im
    given-names: Seonghyuk
    affiliation: "Center for AI and Natural Sciences, Korea Institute for Advanced Study (KIAS)"
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Taeyoung
    affiliation: "School of Computing, Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology (KAIST); School of Computational Sciences, Korea Institute for Advanced Study (KIAS)"
  - family-names: Yang
    given-names: Hongseok
    affiliation: "School of Computing, Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology (KAIST); School of Computational Sciences, Korea Institute for Advanced Study (KIAS)"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mekty2012/OddCycleGoodman-lean"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalisation of the odd-cycle Goodman bound
  t(C_m, W) >= p^m - p(1 - p)^(m - 1) for every graphon W of edge density p and
  every odd m >= 3, together with the strengthened commonality inequality and
  the equality characterisation for p >= 2/3 from the paper "Goodman-type lower
  bounds for odd cycles I: The dense regime".
keywords:
  - Homomorphism densities
  - Goodman bound
  - Graphon
  - Symmetric Polynomial
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
